{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01059",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.9,
      "end_seconds": 6.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "Doctor, hi, where would you like me to put my coat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.03,
      "end_seconds": 11.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.05,
      "end_seconds": 17.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.55,
      "end_seconds": 23.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 25.43,
      "end_seconds": 30.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Doctor, it's been feeling sick. That's what we're worried about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.77,
      "end_seconds": 40.57,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "Okay, can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.18,
      "end_seconds": 47.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "I'd say all the time about a a eight out of ten"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.6,
      "end_seconds": 55.64,
      "duration_seconds": 7.04,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 55.74,
      "end_seconds": 60.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.68,
      "end_seconds": 66.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Mm, I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.04,
      "end_seconds": 71.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Has there been a low fever too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.27,
      "end_seconds": 73.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "mm, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.84,
      "end_seconds": 82.97,
      "duration_seconds": 8.13,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.96,
      "end_seconds": 96.74,
      "duration_seconds": 11.78,
      "text": "A four out of ten, I suppose. I'd say a few times a day. I've also had crampy tummy pain, since last night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.46,
      "end_seconds": 104.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.93,
      "end_seconds": 111.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "It happens once or twice a day. Oh, and watery diarrhoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.37,
      "end_seconds": 115.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.93,
      "end_seconds": 123.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.55,
      "end_seconds": 130.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Alright, take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.71,
      "end_seconds": 133.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "I'd call it severe"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.44,
      "end_seconds": 140.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.7,
      "text": "is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.74,
      "end_seconds": 144.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "I'd say on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.25,
      "end_seconds": 149.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "have you been feeling sick at any time before this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.96,
      "end_seconds": 155.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "A bit, last winter. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 155.9,
      "end_seconds": 158.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "yes, exactly like that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.94,
      "end_seconds": 162.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Okay, I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.13,
      "end_seconds": 173.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.01,
      "end_seconds": 203.96,
      "duration_seconds": 10.95,
      "text": "Okay: weight 66 kilos, pulse is 108 beats a minute. And And BP is 122 over 74, height 181 centimetres, temperature is 38.9 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.16,
      "end_seconds": 207.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.34,
      "end_seconds": 212.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "right, I'll listen to your chest now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.84,
      "end_seconds": 227.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.92,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft with mild general tenderness and your mouth is a little dry."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.33,
      "end_seconds": 230.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.81,
      "end_seconds": 236.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Alright, you can sit up now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.32,
      "end_seconds": 252.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Any severe dehydration or blood in the stool at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.83,
      "end_seconds": 256.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "No, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.67,
      "end_seconds": 261.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "have you had any vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.22,
      "end_seconds": 268.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "No vomiting, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.12,
      "end_seconds": 278.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Alright, on the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.95,
      "end_seconds": 281.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "No, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.19,
      "end_seconds": 285.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.51,
      "end_seconds": 288.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "no changes there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.6,
      "end_seconds": 294.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Right, have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.52,
      "end_seconds": 297.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "No surgery, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.62,
      "end_seconds": 311.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.2,
      "end_seconds": 318.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "I've had COPD for five years now. I have high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.43,
      "end_seconds": 322.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "So, any other things?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 323.09,
      "end_seconds": 328.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "I've had an underactive thyroid for nearly five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.6,
      "end_seconds": 334.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 335.27,
      "end_seconds": 344.15,
      "duration_seconds": 8.88,
      "text": "it's Tiotropium inhaler, once a day. Atorvastatin, 20 milligrams, maybe, at night for my cholesterol"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.45,
      "end_seconds": 349.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 351.2,
      "end_seconds": 355.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "no, it's at home. Thyronorm, 50 micrograms, every morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 356.54,
      "end_seconds": 367.53,
      "duration_seconds": 10.99,
      "text": "doctor, uh, I think the last prescription for the Thyronorm was 100 micrograms we changed it at the last visit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.43,
      "end_seconds": 372.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "hm. Do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 377.01,
      "end_seconds": 385.72,
      "duration_seconds": 8.71,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me. It's oral rehydration salts, 1 sachet, after each loose stool."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.39,
      "end_seconds": 389.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 390.74,
      "end_seconds": 394.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.64,
      "end_seconds": 398.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Are you in work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 399.15,
      "end_seconds": 403.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.57,
      "end_seconds": 409.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 409.76,
      "end_seconds": 411.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "no allergies at all"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 412.23,
      "end_seconds": 421.01,
      "duration_seconds": 8.78,
      "text": "actually, I remember she had some kind of reaction to erythromycin before. I couldn't swear to it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 421.79,
      "end_seconds": 424.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Really? I don't think so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 425.26,
      "end_seconds": 446.75,
      "duration_seconds": 21.49,
      "text": "Alright, so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said. From what you've told me and what I found, the most likely explanation is travellers' diarrhoea. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. It could also be a parasitic infection, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 447.69,
      "end_seconds": 450.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "what are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 451.6,
      "end_seconds": 464.7,
      "duration_seconds": 13.1,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like travellers' diarrhoea, but I'd like to confirm. A stool sample is what I'd like next, for diarrhoea after travel."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 465.72,
      "end_seconds": 467.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Mm, um, alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 468.49,
      "end_seconds": 499.05,
      "duration_seconds": 30.56,
      "text": "drink plenty of fluids and wash your hands carefully and please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose the thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse if that happens, go to emergency we'll catch up if it lasts more than a week that's all from me any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 503.94,
      "end_seconds": 505.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "that's clear, thanks"
    }
  ]
}